  "notes": "USAGE:\nDescribes a very intense, convulsive type of crying characterized by hiccupping and gasping for breath. It is more visceral than simply {泣|な}く (to cry). Most commonly used to describe small children who are crying so hard they cannot stop, but also applies to adults in moments of overwhelming grief or emotion.\n\nThe te-form {泣|な}きじゃくって is the most common form encountered, as the word typically describes an ongoing state.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {泣|な}く: to cry (general, neutral)\n- {泣|な}き{崩|くず}れる: to break down in tears (collapse while crying)\n- すすり{泣|な}く: to weep quietly, to sniffle",
